            <div xml:id="d464">

                <pb facs="0743" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.S1 Monetary Stabilization/15: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hull</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-06-15T21:00:00-04:00">June 15, 1933—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>37. For Secretary of State and Cox and Sprague. The following message is sent for
                    the President. “All kinds of wild reports here about stabilization at some fixed
                    rate, some reports saying around 4 dollars and other reports at other rates. I
                    feel sure all these reports are not founded in any fact. Of course any proposal
                    must in any event come here for approval or disapproval by Treasury Department
                    and me.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
